WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.287
Meet the cylinder.

00:00:01.287 --> 00:00:05.076
A flat top, a curved side, and a shadow on the table.

00:00:05.076 --> 00:00:08.650
Let's see how these become one convincing drawing.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.939
Start with the big structure.

00:00:10.939 --> 00:00:16.121
Compare the height and width, mark the centre, and lightly frame the top and bottom.

00:00:16.121 --> 00:00:18.650
These guides keep your cylinder balanced.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.734
Now shape the ellipses.

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:23.834
A circle seen at an angle looks like an oval.

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:28.450
Keep both ends rounded, then connect the sides with straight lines.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.052
Notice where curve meets flat.

00:00:31.052 --> 00:00:32.944
The top reads as one plane.

00:00:32.944 --> 00:00:36.517
Across the curved side, the tone changes gradually.

00:00:36.517 --> 00:00:39.950
Find the shadow side before adding small details.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.774
Watch the light move.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:46.502
The bright area travels around the curve, while the top changes as a whole.

00:00:46.502 --> 00:00:49.150
The cast shadow falls away from the light.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.431
Build your tones gradually.

00:00:51.431 --> 00:00:56.508
Keep the light side clean, soften the transition, and deepen the shadow band.

00:00:56.508 --> 00:01:01.850
Reflected light can gently lift the far edge, but it still belongs to the shadow.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:05.742
Keep the rim clear where the flat top meets the curve.

00:01:05.742 --> 00:01:10.516
Darken the contact at the base, and soften the cast shadow as it moves away.

00:01:10.516 --> 00:01:12.400
Now your cylinder feels solid.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.841
That's the journey: structure, ellipses, light, and tone.

00:01:16.841 --> 00:01:19.953
You'll follow the teacher one step at a time.

00:01:19.953 --> 00:01:22.650
Get your pencils ready, and let's draw.

